  platform/msm_shared/debug.c:65-110; lk2nd/project/base.mk:47-48.
- `fastboot oem ramoops regions`: prints DEFAULT-window headers; stages nothing.
- `fastboot oem ramoops raw` then `fastboot get_staged ramoops.bin`: snapshots
  exactly the DEFAULT512KiB including headers. No address/size arguments.
  ramoops.c:125-188. No intended source clearing.
- There is no registered `oem ramdump` or `oem lk_log` alias at this pin.

app/aboot/fastboot.c:431-445 stages by copying selected data to scratch START
and setting length;516-540 uploads that staged copy via the upload protocol.
`get_staged` does not resample/select arbitrary memory. Later staging replaces
the snapshot; upload does not clear it. getvar returns registered strings
(447-485), not arbitrary RAM.

EXCLUDE two helpers from an unconditional "safe read-only" recipe:
- ramoops.c:190-203 `oem ramoops console` trusts retained size, ignores signature,
  ring offset and ECC, and does not bound size to the console allocation.
  It can read outside the retained region; a wrapped ring is not reordered.
- ramoops.c:205-246 `oem ramoops dump` handles only the first record, calls
  unbounded memset(scratch,0,record->size) BEFORE checking magic, then may
  copy/decompress, and does not return after failure responses. Malformed
  metadata can corrupt scratch/backing or fault. This is not merely a read.

`oem debug readb/readhw/readl/readq ADDRESS` exists but performs direct virtual
dereferences with alignment checks, not physical mapping or bounded bulk reads
(lk2nd/fastboot/debug/register.c:10-23,61-68).
Default static mappings exclude0xffe00000; blanket identity mapping is disabled
(platform/msm8916/platform.c:62-71,114-148). Do not use these as a supported
vendor-window recovery mechanism. Dynamic runtime mappings were not observed.

## Starting lk2nd is not a proof of preservation

No ramoops startup initializer/persistent writer/header reset exists in this
module. The explicit whole-window clear is the outgoing =zap option.
Normal entry still relocates image/zeros BSS (arch/arm/crt0.S:110-129,175-204),
initializes current boot logging and heap (kernel/main.c:75-101), and sets up
display/boot selection (app/aboot/aboot.c:5539-5564). Automatic boot attempts
can precede fastboot (5652-5687).

The default backing is not excluded from ordinary scratch consumers:
- Fastboot receives full256MiB: aboot.c:5735-5741; downloads write it,
  fastboot.c:487-513.
- Partition fetch writes storage data into the same RAM: lk2nd/fastboot/fetch.c:15-69.
- Boot-image load/decompression: aboot.c:1853-1863,3360-3370.
- Extlinux load/decompression: lk2nd/boot/extlinux.c:540-582.
- Optional simplefb relocation copies framebuffer data near scratch end:
  lk2nd/display/simplefb.c:37-55; not log migration.
Heap is separately bounded by linked-image _end/_end_of_ram
(lib/heap/heap.c:50-58; arch/arm/system-onesegment.ld:90-99), nominally within
the1MiB target image region at0x8f600000.
Preserving FDT reservation-map metadata (lib/libfdt/fdt_rw.c:454-535) does not
make it an allocator exclusion; no such reservation consumer was found in
lk2nd/aboot/target/platform code.

No dedicated write to vendor0xffe00000 was found. That is NOT a retention
guarantee: preceding stock firmware/reset/DDR behavior and hardware-selected
framebuffer placement are unresolved. Continuous splash dynamically maps the
runtime framebuffer (lk2nd/display/cont-splash/target_display.c:15-68).

